## 5. Interactivity & Filters

- **Slicers:** Order Date (between), Region, State, Category, Product, Discount band.
  Sync slicers across all pages via *Format → Edit Interactions* / Sync Slicers pane.
- **Drill-through page:** Build a "Product Detail" drill-through page — right-click a
  product bar on Page 2 to jump into a detailed view (trend, top customers for that
  product, region split).
- **Cross-filtering:** Keep default cross-highlighting so clicking a Region bar filters
  the Category donut and product table.
- **Bookmarks:** Add a "Reset Filters" button (Bookmark + Home icon) on each page.
- **Tooltips:** Build a custom tooltip page showing Sales, Profit, and Margin % on hover
  for chart data points.

---

## 6. Visual Design Guidelines

- **Color palette:** One primary brand color (e.g., navy `#1F4E78`) for Sales, a
  secondary accent (e.g., teal `#2E9E8E`) for Profit, and a neutral gray for Cost —
  keep consistent across all pages.
- **Typography:** Segoe UI (Power BI default) throughout; bold only for KPI numbers and
  titles.
- **Layout:** 16:9 canvas, consistent margins, KPI cards top-aligned, slicers pinned
  left in a shaded panel.
- **Conditional formatting:** Red/amber/green on Margin % and YoY % to instantly flag
  underperformance.
- **Accessibility:** Ensure color contrast, add alt text to visuals, avoid relying on
  color alone (use data labels).

---

## 7. Business Insights to Surface

- Identify which **category drives the most profit** vs. the most revenue (they may
  differ — margin mix matters).
- Flag **products with high sales but low margin** (candidates for pricing review).
- Show whether **higher discount bands correlate with lower overall margin** — useful
  for setting discount policy.
- Highlight **top vs. bottom performing regions/states** to guide territory planning.
- Distinguish **repeat customers vs one-time buyers** to inform retention strategy.
- Surface **seasonality** (Nov–Dec spike) to guide inventory and staffing plans.

